5450:<a id="turn-hook-not-loaded"></a>
5451-
5452:`turn_hook_not_loaded`: the per-turn hook that puts "check GBrain first"
5453-beside every user turn is not running in the harness. Agents use the brain
5454-when that rule reaches them on every turn; the MCP tool list or an
5455-instruction file alone rarely gets the brain used. The `reason` says what
5456-the install check found:
5457-
5458-- `missing`: no gbrain per-turn hook is configured for the harness.
5459-- `untrusted`: the hook is configured but the harness will not run it yet
5460-  (Codex: no matching trust entry, trust it in `/hooks`; OpenClaw:
5461-  `hooks.allowConversationAccess` is off; Hermes: the command is not in
5462-  `shell-hooks-allowlist.json`).
5463-- `hook_failed`: the Claude Code or Codex hook command exited non-zero.
5464-- `no_rule`: the hook ran but added no rule, usually because the
5465-  brain-first block for that harness was opted out.
5466-- `not_loaded`: the harness's own check does not show the hook loaded.
5467-
5468-Run `fix.argv` (it re-runs the install that writes the hook), then check
5469-with the harness's own command:
5470-
5471-| Harness | Check |
5472-|---|---|
5473-| Claude Code | `/hooks` in a session lists the UserPromptSubmit hook |
5474-| Codex | `/hooks` in a session; trust the hook there if it asks |
5475-| OpenClaw | `openclaw plugins inspect gbrain-turn-rule --runtime --json` shows it loaded with `before_prompt_build` |
5476-| Hermes | `hermes hooks doctor` shows the `pre_llm_call` hook healthy |
5477-
5478-`gbrain doctor --only harness_wiring --json` reports the same state per
5479-harness. opencode and Cursor have no per-turn hook gbrain can install; the
5480-rule reaches them through their instruction file only.
5481-
5482-### Hook starts gbrain in the session directory

